  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/BackSurfaceReEctor": {
    "mds:value": "reduction rear recombination",
    "mds:quote": "This is a low-cost step since usually done in conjunction with the required edge-junction isolation step."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/CellStructure": {
    "mds:value": "PERC cell; UNSW planar PESC cell",
    "mds:quote": "The attractive feature was the elegant way in which the PERC cell incorporated three attributes into the rear contacting scheme that earlier work at UNSW and elsewhere had shown were important to obtaining high ef ﬁciency. These were … with simultaneously increased rear surface re ﬂection by use of a dielectrically displaced rear metal re ﬂector."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/CellPerformance": {
    "mds:value": "flat-plate photovoltaic module ef ﬁ ciency (19.9% certi fied in 1992, equivalent to 20.1%, under present standards)",
    "mds:quote": "Sixteen of these early PERC hybrid cells were encapsulated into a nominally 800-cm  module in 1992 resulting in the rst con rmed 20% t-plate photovoltaic module ef ciency (19.9% certi ed in 1992, equivalent to .1%, under present standards)"
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/ContactMaterial": {
    "mds:value": "Al (aluminum) alloy; metal-semiconductor contact area",
    "mds:quote": "The attractive feature was the elegant way in which the PERC cell incorporated three attributes into the rear contacting scheme that earlier work at UNSW and elsewhere had shown were important to obtaining high ef ﬁciency."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/CrystallineStructure": {
    "mds:value": "monocrystalline; multicrystalline",
    "mds:quote": "Applying the approach to multicrystalline substrates led to the ﬁrst multicrystalline cell of ef ﬁciency above 20%, by present standards, in 1998 [5]."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/DielectricSurfacePassivation": {
    "mds:value": "oxide passivation; dielectric oxide",
    "mds:quote": "The key issues in the development of this technology included … trying to understand these data (later realising drop at high temperature was due to surface roughening and consequent light-trapping), expected reﬂection values were calculated theoretically."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Dopants": {
    "mds:value": "boron; chlorine",
    "mds:quote": "This proved more challenging than for the phosphorus diffusions already established. Some tips from the solar cell group at Stanford University regarding the advantages of chlorine-based furnace processing proved most helpful here,"
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Efficiency": {
    "mds:value": "21.8%",
    "mds:quote": "These initial results fuelled the ongoing improvements in silicon cell ef ﬁciency on p-type monocrystalline substrates to 25% (Figure 9)."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/EmitterDesign": {
    "mds:value": "inverted rear emitter structure",
    "mds:quote": "much later in 2005, an inverted rear"
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/EquipmentConfigurations": {
    "mds:value": "hybrid sequence, using laser processing for the top cell surface but chemical etching to open holes in the rear oxide",
    "mds:quote": "PERC integration was achieved by a hybrid sequence, using laser processing for the top cell surface but chemical etching to open holes in the rear oxide , with hole positions de ned by photolithography."
  },
  "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/InterfacePassivation": {
